<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Athanasios the Athonite</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 920–c. 1003</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Athanasius the Athonite</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Athanasios the Athonite was a Byzantine monk who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lavra">Great Lavra</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-athos">Mount Athos</a> in 963 with the support of his friend Nikephoros Phokas, later emperor. It was the first large organised monastery on the peninsula, and his rules shaped Athonite monasticism. He is venerated as a saint in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox Church</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/athanasios-the-athonite.jpg" alt="Athanasios the Athonite" width="320" height="496" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Manuel Panselinos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Athanasios.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
